.TH geectl-remote-upload-file 1  "geectl-remote-upload-file 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-upload\-file \- Upload a file into a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the upload. The local file is read from `\-\-from`; `\-\-binary` uploads bytes instead of text
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote upload\-file\fR [\fB\-\-binary\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-from\fR> <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Upload a file into a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the upload. The local file is read from `\-\-from`; `\-\-binary` uploads bytes instead of text
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
The local file to read the content from
.TP
\fB\-\-binary\fR
Upload bytes instead of text: a binary file uploads instead of failing the UTF\-8 check a text upload would hit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package lives in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to upload into
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
The file name on the server
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
